<section class="teaser-collection section-wrap collection--two-columns">
<div class="collection__items">
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Making your graduate education affordable</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>In addition to scholarships and financial aid, more than 30 percent of full-time graduate students hold assistantships or departmental fellowships amounting to more than $4 million each year.</p>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="{{f:22379530}}"> <span>Financial Aid and Funding Opportunities</span> </a><a class=" link--rich" href="{{f:22391027}}"><span>Cost of Attendance</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Admission to the program</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>Full admission to the MACC professional curriculum requires:</p>
<ol>
<li>An undergraduate degree in accounting, or the functional equivalent, from an AACSB-accredited institution.</li>
<li>An overall grade point average (GPA) of 3.20 on a 4.00 scale.</li>
<li>A grade of <em>B</em> (3.0) or better in all undergraduate accounting courses.</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="http://catalog.wichita.edu/graduate/w-frank-barton-business/accounting/macc-master-accountancy/"> <span>Admission requirements</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="teaser-collection section-wrap collection--two-columns section-wrap--nipple-down">
<div class="collection__items">
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Curriculum</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>The MACC program requires a minimum of 30 hours depending on your academic background. Students without a bachelor's degree in accounting can expect to complete additional hours for their MACC degree.</p>
<p>In addition to the traditional master's degree in accounting, the Barton School also offers two specialized concentrations: accounting information systems (AIS) and taxation.</p>
<p>Courses are offered during the evening to accommodate adult learners.</p>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="http://catalog.wichita.edu/graduate/w-frank-barton-business/accounting/macc-master-accountancy/#requirementstext"> <span>View the curriculum</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Careers</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>A graduate degree in accountancy from Wichita State's Barton School will help you take the next step in your career &mdash; while opening doors to new career possibilities.</p>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/business-and-financial/accountants-and-auditors.htm#tab-1"> <span>Learn more about careers in this field</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
